## 1 2. Experimental
2.1. Chemicals. Zinc nitrate hexahydrate $(\mathrm{Zn}(\mathrm{NO}_{3})_{2}{\cdot}6\mathrm{H}_{2}\mathrm{O}$ , $99\%$ ) and cobalt chloride $(\mathrm{CoCl}_{2})$ were purchased from Sigma-Aldrich Chemical Co. 2-Methylimidazole (MeIm, purity $99\%$ ), hydrofluoric acid, and methanol were obtained from Nacalai Tesque Reagent Co. All the chemicals were used without further purification.
2.2. Preparation of ZIF-8 seeds with different particle sizes. In a typical synthesis of ZIF-8 with a diameter of ${\sim}4~\upmu\mathrm{m}$ , methanolic solutions of zinc nitrate hexahydrate ( $810.4~\mathrm{mg}$ , $40~\mathrm{ml}$ ) and methanolic solutions of MeIm $\mathrm{\cdot526~mg,~40~ml}$ were mixed under stirring. Then the mixture was transferred into an autoclave and was kept at $100^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for 12 hours. The white powder was collected by centrifugation, washed several times with methanol, and dried at $80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . When the mixed methanolic solution of zinc nitrate hexahydrate and MeIm was kept at room temperature $(22^{\circ}\mathrm{C})$ for 12 hours, the white particles of ZIF-8 with a diameter of $500\ \mathrm{nm}$ were precipitated. The size of ZIF-8 could be further decreased to ${\sim}50~\mathrm{nm}$ by adding polyvinyl pyrrolidone (PVP) as the capping agent and kept the reaction at room temperature.
2.3. Preparation of ZIF-67. In the synthesis of ZIF-67 with a diameter of ${\sim}5\upmu\mathrm{m}$ , a methanolic solutions (80 ml) of cobalt chloride $(519~\mathrm{mg})$ , polyvinyl pyrrolidone (PVP) $\mathrm{\Delta\langle600~mg\rangle}$ and MeIm $(2630~\mathrm{mg})$ ) were mixed under stirring. Then the mixture was kept reaction at room temperature for 12 hours. The bright purple powder of ZIF-67 was collected by centrifugation, washed several times with methanol, and dried at $80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . 2.4. Preparation of core–shell ZIF-8 $@$ ZIF-67 crystals. In a typical synthesis of core–shell ZIF-8 $@$ ZIF-67 crystals with micrometer-size, ZIF-8 seeds $\mathrm{80~mg}$ ) with diameter of ${\sim}4~\upmu\mathrm{m}$ were first well dispersed in methanol ( $10~\mathrm{mL}$ ) under sonication for $30~\mathrm{min}$ . After stirring for $20~\mathrm{min}$ , a methanolic solution of cobalt chloride (176.6 mg, $3~\mathrm{mL}$ ) and a methanolic solution of MeIm $\mathrm{895~mg,3~mL}$ ) were stepwise injected into the above mixture. After stirring for another $5\mathrm{{min}}$ , the mixture was transferred into an autoclave and kept at $100^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ for 12 hours. During this time, the core–shell ZIF-8 $@$ ZIF-67 crystals were obtained. After cooling to room temperature, the resulting sample was collected by centrifugation, washed several times with methanol, and dried at $80^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ . The molar ratio of $\mathrm{Co}^{2+}/\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}$ in the obtained ZIF-8@ZIF67 crystals under these typical conditions was 0.26. The shell thickness of ZIF-67 can be tuned by changing the amounts of methanolic solutions of cobalt chloride and MeIm. The obtained core–shell ZIF-8 $@$ ZIF-67 crystals with
