## 1 Conclusion
Core-shell ZIF-8 $@$ ZIF-67 crystals, which integrate the properties of single ZIF-8 and ZIF-67, are elaborately designed for the first time by applying a seed-mediated growth technique. The core sizes of ZIF8 and the shell thicknesses of ZIF-67 can be tuned simply by using different sizes of ZIF-8 seeds and varying the feeding molar ratios of $\mathrm{Co}^{2+}/\mathrm{Zn}^{2+}$ . After the direct carbonization of core–shell ZIF-8 $@$ ZIF-67 crystals, a new type of selectively functionalized $\mathsf{N C@G C}$ composites retain both the high surface area (up to $1276~\mathrm{m}^{2}{\cdot}\mathrm{g}^{-1})$ and high $\mathrm{\DeltaN}$ content $(10.6~\mathrm{wt\%})$ ) derived from core ZIF-8 and superior graphitic structure originated from shell ZIF-67. The optimized NC@GC exhibits a distinguished electrochemical performance as an electrode in supercapacitors. This study not only bridges diverse carbon-based materials with infinite MOFs but also opens a new avenue for artificially designed nanoarchitectures with target functionalities.
